    artifact "perf-results/2026-10-25-internet/handoff.json"
    summary """
        Ubuntu 26.04.1, i7-13700H, rustc 1.99.0, release, IPv4-only Wi-Fi (no VPN, no IPv6 route), user-permitted torrent. The client added the .torrent from its own info dictionary and found peers through DHT and PEX; the Ubuntu tracker gave 1 peer over IPv4. First verified piece at 50.3 s; complete and seeding at 519 s, 6482409472 of 6482409472 bytes, average 12.5 MB/s, peak 19.6 MB/s, peak 47 peers, peak RSS 36.4 MB, 0 hash failures, 0 steps over 500 ms. An independent Python pass checked 24729 of 24729 piece SHA-1s with 0 mismatches; the ISO SHA-256 is 601e30fbf5d97759367c632e2c33630665039b7e2158fd068403da3ccf1bda1f. The log has counts and rates only. The code at d6709ad failed this add in 3.9 s (baseline.log).
